WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.500
Bring Back the Bond Between Father and Son!

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.500
Evilmon's Bewitchment

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.010
Bring Back the Bond Between Father and Son!

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.500
Evilmon's Bewitchment!

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.640
What? There's data you're interested in investigating?

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.220
Yes.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.470
What is it?

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.390
I have no real proof yet, so...

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.560
Is that why you're asking for time off?

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.180
Yes.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.760
Please give me some time.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.800
Very well.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:22.730
You have my permission.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.360
Will we be able to find the answer?

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.570
We'll do our very best to find it.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:32.340
Without fail.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.730
What?

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:39.280
He's on break in America?!

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.610
Aniki, what's an America?

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.630
Why's he the only one who gets a vacation?!

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.270
I wonder how easygoing he can get...

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.830
Hey, don't ignore me, Aniki...

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.160
I wanted to go, too...

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.340
To the sunny West Coast!

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.870
So, what's this America?

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.300
Is it tasty?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.130
Of course not!

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.780
Now, now, let's have snack time!

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:04.240
Our sweets for today are Kyoto's distinguished legendary items:

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:10.910
NOTE: <i>Manjuu</i> (饅頭) are steamed buns that are usually filled with anko (sweet bean paste).

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.230
Suzaku manjuu!

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.230
I know those! They're famous, aren't they?

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.910
It's really hard to get them!

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:11.620
Huh?

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:12.730
What's wrong?

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.150
Oh no, it's empty!

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.610
Yeah, I already ate those.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.420
What?!

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.700
They weren't bad, but they were a little tiny.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.790
I don't believe this!

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.770
Agumon-chan, follow me for a second.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.580
What? Are you gonna feed me more?

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:29.810
You pig!!

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:32.020
We lined up at 5 AM to be able to get these!

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.630
Apologize! I'll never forgive you for hogging them all!

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.590
How are you going to make up for this?!

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.550
Take responsibility!!

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.930
The follower's failures are his aniki's failures.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.770
Aniki'll take responsibility for me!

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:45.580
Huh?

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.140
Me?!

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.260
Oh, really?

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:51.980
Masaru, you'll settle the deal for your follower, won't you?

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.020
Aniki...

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.990
So what are you going to do, Aniki?

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.080
F-Fine, it's just manjuu.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.780
Have you heard about Shiratori's?

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.700
The one that has a long waiting list of orders?

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:04.700
NOTE: <i>Shiratori</i> means "White Bird."

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.700
Their Shiratori manjuu is famous!

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.830
It's actually my friend's place.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.350
I'll buy Japan's best manjuu there for you.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:12.210
Shiratori Retreat

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.920
Zaisen-san, please let me off today with this.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:18.820
Aniki, are you gonna be okay?

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.760
It doesn't matter how popular they are. They'll make 10 or 20 manjuu for me whenever I ask.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.890
Hey, is that old man Shiratori?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.530
W-Wait!

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.570
Please stop!

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.200
It's your fault!

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.860
But there's no helping this matter!

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.960
Shiratori-san, you've got to fully pay back what I've loaned you.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.370
Or else things will become troublesome for me, too.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.660
Give me one more week... no, three more days, please!

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.130
Quit your babblin'!

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.720
B-But I never said that I <i>wouldn't</i>  pay you back!

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.230
Are you makin' light of this?!

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:49.940
Hold it right there.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:50.580
Who's that?

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.430
Just a customer who came here to buy manjuu.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.810
Moron, let go!

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.050
You're making the manjuu lose their flavor!

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.570
Get lost!

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.600
Remember this!

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.520
Let's go!

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:05.420
Damn it!

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.040
Are you okay, Dad?

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:08.760
Yeah.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.990
Thank you very much.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.160
Nah, they just looked like troublemakers...

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.120
Huh? Masaru?

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.040
Koichiro, do you know him?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.680
Yeah, he's my friend.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.280
It's been a while. What's up, Masaru?

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.280
Yo! I actually have a request.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.560
I came here to buy Japan's best Shiratori manjuu.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.170
We're not making them anymore.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:30.800
What?

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:31.750
Why?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.470
I saw you guys on TV!

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.510
There was a huge crowd in front of the store...

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:36.710
You guys were doing great!

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.890
When the media started praising us, a lot of customers came here every day.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:45.010
But the boom ended really quickly.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.370
Mom got sick,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.680
Although it is discourteous of us, our business will be shutdown for some time. (Shiratori Retreat‘s Owner)

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.560
and when we closed the store for half a month...

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.910
the customers just stopped coming.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.470
My dad lost his motivation,

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:55.530
and he stopped making the Shiratori manjuu.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.150
That's not good!

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:59.890
It's no use no matter what I tell him.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:03.110
Even those guys you saw today... it's Dad's fault, since he's borrowed money from them.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.410
I see.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.070
But in the past, he looked like he had a lot of fun making sweets...

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.560
We can't go back until we get Japan's best manjuu, Aniki.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.000
Huh?

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.650
Ah, nothing. Just thinking out loud.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:19.610
I've gotta do something to encourage the old man and make him bring back the Shiratori manjuu!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.600
But...

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.770
Don't worry.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:24.010
Just leave everything to the great Daimon Masaru-sama!

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.960
Do I have anything of value in here?

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.250
Money... I need money.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:31.770
Anything will work!

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.060
Isn't there anything I can sell?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.230
Damn it! I should have some scroll paintings in here!

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.480
Where are they? I need money!

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:45.740
Wh-What?

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.790
Need money.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.580
Need money.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.440
The Shiratori manjuu aren't here yet...

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.810
That Masaru... when he comes back, he'll be severely punished.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:12.500
There was a faint signal in Point C-307.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.400
What could it be?

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.860
It disappeared...

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:16.330
Could it be a Digimon signal?

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.490
I don't know... maybe it's just static.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:21.850
By the way, isn't Sector C where the Shiratori Retreat is located?

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.300
Has Masaru bought the manjuu yet?

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:27.010
We ended up having no snacks today.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.210
Kurosaki-san, don't be so bitter.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.040
Did I hear something?

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:30.790
Oh, nothing!

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.270
Since I'm a little worried, I'll go patrolling in Sector C!

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.530
If you spot Masaru, drag him back!

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:36.430
You got it!

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.000
Dad, don't!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.730
Move!

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:40.440
I need money!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.130
Dad!

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.740
Don't do this! That money is for this month's bills...!

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:45.550
Shut up!

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.410
5-6-8!

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.660
5-6-8!

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:48.860
Dad...!

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.860
What's happened to your old man?

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:52.820
He's acting kinda weird...

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.720
He must be off to gamble again.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.230
Gamble?

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:59.830
That's the reason why we've gotten into so much debt.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.240
I see.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.190
But there's something else...

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.600
Have you gotten the Shiratori manjuu yet?

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:07.750
Kurosaki-san is in a rage.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.710
Perfect timing!

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.140
What do you mean by that?

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.350
Never mind, hurry up!

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.330
Why?

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.680
C'mon, go after that car!

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.540
Go after <i>which</i>  car?

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.010
Koichiro, leave everything to me!

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:23.310
Masaru?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.630
It's been a long time, Professor Stimson.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:37.030
Welcome. Thank you for coming.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.290
I'm sorry for the sudden intrusion.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.250
If I can be of service to you, it will be an honor.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.050
The tenth race will begin shortly.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.030
Why did we have to come to the race track?

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.360
I'll explain later.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.220
We need to find old man Shiratori!

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.060
Find him?

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.220
In this crowd?

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.050
I'm counting on you, Gouya-chan!

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:01.180
2-8! Go 2-8!

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:02.940
5-6-8!

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:04.390
5-6-8!

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:05.980
5-6-8!

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:25.580
PicoDevimon

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:25.580
Child Level

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:17.920
PicoDevimon.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.050
A mischievious Child Level Digimon who plays evil tricks.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:25.580
For its special attack, it throws its syringes, Pico Darts.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.330
Let's go, men!

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.250
Sir!

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.530
Yes, sir!

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.330
5-6-8!

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:36.640
5-6-8!

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.420
5-6-8!

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:47.950
Get ready, men!

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:48.470
Sir!

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:49.260
Yes, sir!

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:54.300
Pick your animal.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:54.650
Sir!

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:55.270
Yes, sir!

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:56.210
Number 8 is mine!

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.050
Number 6!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:57.660
Number 5!

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.740
We've entered the last length!

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:00.730
5-6-8!

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:01.660
5-6-8!

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:02.980
Pico Darts!

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:04.580
Pico Darts!

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:12.460
Crap!

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:15.460
What's this?!

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:19.890
Number 7 Shirohara Jupiter, Number 6 Poppo Hatomura, and Number 8 Rocket Yuta are gaining speed!

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:19.890
It's turned into <i>7</i> -6-8!

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.220
Yoshino!

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.970
I sense a Digimon around here!

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:23.810
Huh? Where?

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.390
I don't know...

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.810
There are too many people here for me to pinpoint...

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:29.580
What's wrong?

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.290
There's apparently a Digimon around, but we don't know for sure.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.060
A Digimon?

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:35.200
I don't feel anything...

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.500
Aniki, I'm hungry!

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.470
Yeah, we haven't eaten anything.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.020
I do feel it! There's a Digimon around here somewhere!

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:42.890
For real?

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.010
There's something strange about this...

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:46.030
Hurry! All of us together!

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:46.620
Sir!

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:47.500
Yes, sir!

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.080
Number 5 Kaizer Leona is pulling off an incredible spurt!

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.300
5-6-8!

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.340
5-6-8!

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:07.230
I got it!

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.230
Phew. It worked out.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.050
I did it! I did it!

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.150
I really won!

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.040
Whoa, this is freaky.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.970
I really do feel a Digimon around here!

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.030
Is it a strong one?

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:21.980
Good work, everyone!

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:22.470
Sir!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:23.580
Yes, sir!

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:24.620
It disappeared!

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.270
I can't sense it anymore!

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.520
Something's odd.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:30.250
Let's go back to HQ and investigate this.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.850
I'll stay here.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:32.490
Huh?

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.790
I made a promise.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:37.510
Until I find the old man and get him to make manjuu, I won't go back!

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:40.470
Hey, do you understand what you're saying here?

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.390
A man doesn't go back on his word!

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:44.350
Lookin' good, Aniki!

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.320
Let's go, Yoshino.

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:48.220
Yeah.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:49.310
I can't deal with any more stupidity.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.820
A Digimon signal hasn't been detected.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:04.820
Except for the static that appeared when Yoshino left to patrol, nothing has been confirmed today.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:05.960
I see.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:06.830
That's strange.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:09.240
But I'm sure of it!

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:12.250
It was weak, but I'm sure I felt a Digimon signal!

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.540
We will have to look more thoroughly into this.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:16.450
Yoshino.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.710
Keep a close eye on Sector C where the static first appeared.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.210
Roger!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.770
Thank you! Thank you!

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.770
Now I can pay off my debts!

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:33.910
It's all thanks to you, God of Good Fortune!

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:36.700
Thank you! Thank you!

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:41.100
Please lend me your power once again! I beg you!

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.820
Did your old man go off to gamble again?

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:23.890
Yeah.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.030
This is worrisome.

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:25.900
It's all right.

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:27.160
What's wrong, Koichiro?

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:30.680
My dream to run our Japanese sweet store...

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.160
I've already given it up.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:34.290
Well, I won't!

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.620
I'm not leaving until he's made manjuu for me!

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.890
Even if you say that, I think it'll be impossible to fulfill.

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:42.080
No, it won't! It's the end once you give up!

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.760
Yo, Koichiro.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.090
Dad! How did you get this car?!

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:51.060
Isn't it obvious? It's a gift from the God of Good Fortune.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:53.140
The God of Good Fortune?

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:55.460
Can you really afford an expensive car like this?

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.710
Yeah, I can.

00:12:57.530 --> 00:13:00.020
Here's some change. Use it to buy something to eat, you two.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:02.510
Please, stop gambling already!

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.490
That's right, mister! Make those delicious manjuu of yours again!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.380
Are you kidding me?

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:09.520
Gambling's more fun than making that manjuu!

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:10.630
Adios!

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:12.900
Mister!

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.730
Shiratori manjuu, huh?

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:27.400
I tried making them myself yesterday, but it didn't go too well.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.470
Do you use that wooden molding to make them?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.050
Yeah.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:36.360
You carve out the shape of a bird in this, then you put the manjuu in here and mold it before baking.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:39.280
You have to be careful not to let it tear or the bean paste inside will spill out. It's actually pretty tough to make.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:43.070
Dad made it look easy. It just shows how good he is...

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.400
He looked really cool when he was working.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.980
I wish I'd learned how to make these earlier.

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:50.630
"Dad," huh?

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.790
So this is it, Masaru.

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:58.850
Since I can't make them myself, just give up on the Shiratori manjuu.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.830
I told you, I won't give up.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:02.000
Masaru?

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.570
What's the deal with this God of Good Fortune he talked about?

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:09.130
He tells me to stay out of there, so I'm not really sure...

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:11.340
but I think he sits in that room, praying in the darkness.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:14.310
Praying in the darkness?

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:15.900
Is this the place?

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.000
We'll get in trouble if Dad finds out!

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.480
Don't worry!

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:20.590
Masaru!

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:21.880
Don't do this!

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.210
C'mon, Masaru!

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.320
Is that the God of Good Fortune?

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:29.610
Man, it looks nasty!

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.570
Does this thing really have God's grace in it?

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:33.740
Ow!

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:36.320
Why are <i>you</i>  crying out in pain, Agumon?

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:37.950
It's not me, Aniki.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:39.210
It can't be...

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:42.630
Did this thing talk?!

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:43.780
Hey!

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:44.840
Dad!

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:47.100
Don't get too close to the Great God of Good Fortune!

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:48.130
Stop, Dad!

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.760
As long as I have the Great God of Good Fortune, I can get as much money as I want!

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.510
I won't hand over this wonderful God to anyone!

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:57.000
I don't need that weird statue thing.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.640
I just wanted to see it because it looked suspicious.

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:00.900
Dad...

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.430
What's happened to you?

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.920
Why aren't you making sweets again?!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.390
I have money now!

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:08.150
There's no need for me to run around and work anymore!

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:10.010
As long as I have money, I can get anything I want!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.930
I can fool around for the rest of my life!

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.210
Dad...

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:14.280
Hold it!

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.990
There are things you can never get with money!

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.640
You can't buy hope with money!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.890
You can't just buy a kid's dreams with cash!

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:28.150
Koichiro's dream is to follow in your footsteps and make Japanese sweets!

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:31.220
And yet, here you are trying to crush his dream!

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:36.270
Children grow up watching their parents' backs!

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:37.820
So, you know...

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:41.350
That's why parents can't turn their backs on their children's dreams!

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.350
Shut up!

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:47.980
Shut up, shut up!

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:48.980
Who cares?

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:51.810
Who gives a damn about dreams?! This store can be destroyed for all I care!

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:52.720
Dad!

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:58.700
Yoshino, I sense a Digimon signal!

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.470
It's really close this time!

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:01.660
Okay.

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:08.570
The money!

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.550
Great God of Good Fortune...!

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.620
Dad, look out!

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.630
He's not a God of Good Fortune!

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:14.260
He's a Digimon!

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:15.890
A Digimon?

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:28.560
Evilmon

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:28.560
Adult Level

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:20.850
Evilmon.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:24.530
An Adult Level Digimon that loves to torture others.

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.340
His special attack is Nightmare Shock.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.560
Those who are hit with it will have a nightmare they'll never wake up from!

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:31.530
Dad, are you okay?!

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:33.820
Agumon, Realize!

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:37.870
Let's rock, Aniki!

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.420
Who are these guys?

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.790
There's a Digimon signal in Sector C, Point-307!

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:46.750
We've found a match on the data.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:48.710
It's Evilmon and PicoDevimon!

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:50.710
He's removed his sleep mode!

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.060
He must have put himself into a dormant state,

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:55.340
which enabled him to escape initially from under our noses...

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.640
Tell Yoshino to stay on her guard!

00:16:58.570 --> 00:16:59.300
Roger!

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:03.620
Understood.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:05.100
I'm heading there to secure them right now.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.420
This is the worst.

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:12.840
Destroy it!

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:13.620
Destroy it!

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:14.380
Destroy it!

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:15.740
The money!

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:17.470
Stop! Don't do this!

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:18.590
Destroy it!

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:21.910
Stop that!

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:24.110
I'll stop 'em!

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:25.630
Baby Flame!

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.030
What selfish brats you are!

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:29.340
We're just doing what we're told!

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:29.920
What?

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:31.880
We're destroying it because he said to destroy it!

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.290
We gave him money because he said he wanted it!

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:36.090
Man, you humans are so selfish!

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:38.890
Dad, it's dangerous!

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:37.980
The money...!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.340
The money...!

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:40.490
Shut up!

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.240
I'll just stomp all of you to death!

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.310
Give it up!

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:44.140
Hurry!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:45.810
Agumon!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:46.710
Yeah!

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.210
Baby Flame!

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.280
Koichiro, stay back!

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.930
You pesky pipsqueak!

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:55.450
Agumon!

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:56.940
Aniki!

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:58.910
Let go of me, jerkface!

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.870
You're not getting in my way!

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.690
Nuts Shoot!

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.420
What do you think you're doing?

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.290
Thanks, Yoshino!

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.240
Eliminate them!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:12.250
Sir! Yes, Sir!

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.230
Don't get in our way!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:19.220
Take that!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.150
Lalamon!

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.640
Baby Flame!

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:23.470
Whoa!

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:24.180
Close one!

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:27.140
Evilmon! Close in on them and crush them all!

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:29.600
Yes! Leave it to me!

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:31.460
Cut the crap!

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:35.020
I'm not getting beat up by a loser like you!

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:36.130
Shut up!

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.740
You sure are an annoying punk!

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:40.580
Damn, now you've <i>really</i>  pissed me off!

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:48.220
Let's go, Agumon!

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:49.210
Aniki!

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:54.700
Digisoul Charge!

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:01.050
Agumon, evolve!

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:08.330
GeoGreymon!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.440
You got bigger before I could trample you.

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.590
Turn yourself in quietly, Evilmon!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.030
Yeah, right!

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:18.140
Nightmare Shock!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.660
I won't get fooled by something like that!

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:28.730
What?

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.630
Mega Burst!

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.540
Wha-! Evilmon!

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:43.190
R-Run!

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:44.620
Sir! Yes, Sir!

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.420
Mega Flame!

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:52.290
Okay!

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.190
Securing completed.

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:57.340
We bagged four at once.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.150
Though they made a big mess...

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:03.170
Th-The money... all of it burned to ash...

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:04.850
Who cares about the money?

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.790
We still have the store.

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:09.160
Let's make manjuu again, Dad!

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.120
Koichiro...

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:15.430
I want you to teach me how to make the Shiratori manjuu.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:19.090
I'll do whatever you ask and help you out with everything! I want to make manjuu!

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:21.100
Koichiro...

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:25.020
I really want to make Japanese sweets for a living!

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:26.170
Is that so...

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:28.050
Dad...

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:31.020
Okay, I'll teach you.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.920
I'll teach you everything!

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:33.750
Dad!

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:38.030
Delicious!

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:40.020
This is more than what I expected of Shiratori manjuu!

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.490
They look cute, and they have such a refined taste!

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:46.130
You made us wait a long time, but I forgive you.

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:47.740
They're really good!

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:49.950
I'm going to buy more no matter how long I have to wait for it.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:54.420
Because of the Digimon, these delicious manjuu were about to disappear forever.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:58.890
Evilmon was resting in a dormant state, so his Digimon signal was untraceable.

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:02.380
When I first saw him, he just looked like a stone statue.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:05.340
We will have to be very cautious from now on.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:09.080
Captain! I think I discovered something amazing.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:09.670
What is it?

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:10.920
I figured it out!

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:14.570
The Digimon may be appearing because they're reacting to human greed.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:17.350
That's not all!

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:18.900
Tohma!

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:20.850
When'd you come back?

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:24.200
Captain, after studying all of the Digimon cases that have occurred,

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.650
I've come upon something very important.

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:31.030
Please send out an emergency notification to all DATS divisions!

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:33.650
An emergency notification?

